From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jens Willmer <info@jwillmer.de>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 12:21:05 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 080/110] Markdown preview positions are measured, not
 estimated

The scroll sync and the outline in Preview placed each line by an
estimate of the drawn heights, which was wrong around images and closed
<details> (counted by their source length). Each top-level element of the
preview is now drawn in its own container; after every parse, resize or
<details> toggle a widget operation reads where each one was laid out.
Between two measured elements a line takes its share of the space by its
estimated height. The estimate only stands in before the first layout.

The outline in Preview highlights the first heading whose top is in view,
and a preview scrolled by the user puts the first line in view at the top
of the editor, blank lines skipped.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

